```mdl
decision D-127: ECHO and PLEX have Build with a coding agent as the third page in Start here; HALO has none yet. PLEX's replaces Build a plugin with the assistant, whose route redirects to it. The page's prompt is a text box the reader edits before opening it in Claude Code (`claude://code/new?q=`), Codex (`codex://new?prompt=`) or Cursor (`cursor://anysphere.cursor-deeplink/prompt?text=`). PLEX's prompt starts with a fixed line that tells the agent to use the `composer-plugin-dev` skill, or to read it from the repository when it is not installed, since none of the three links can install a plugin. Its default text is the eval's World Clock brief without "test it yourself": the skill's default flow ends with the reader enabling the dev server, which needs no debug port.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.4, echo-build-with-agent, plex-build-with-agent, app-framework-welcome]
  why: The `composer-plugin-dev` eval shows the skill plus a one-line brief builds a working plugin in 5 to 7 minutes for about $0.50, and readers use more than one coding agent.
  rejected:
    - An install link per agent: Claude's links only prefill a prompt; Codex's plugin-install link takes a Codex marketplace, which the `dxos` plugin is not in.
```

```mdl
decision D-128: Agents may read a whole section in one fetch: `llms-full.txt` holds every page of it, examples included. A page must not assume an agent reads one page at a time, or that an example on one page is unknown to an agent reading another.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.1]
  why: The `composer-plugin-dev` eval's agent reads the plugin guide, whose World Clock example matches its brief, so the eval measures how well an agent follows the guide.
```

```mdl
decision D-129: The plugin guide keeps World Clock as its worked example, as the eval's guide-following case. New worked examples stay off the subjects the eval holds out, such as a habit tracker or a standup board; Bookmarks (PLEX learning path), Contacts (ECHO tutorial) and Notes (the Open in Claude prompt) are already taken. Check with the eval's owner before adding a plugin example.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-build-with-agent]
  why: An example that matches a held-out brief lets the agent copy the answer, and the eval stops measuring what it is meant to.
```

```mdl
decision D-130: Build with a coding agent replaces the Open in Claude pages, and the Agents groups go with them; their routes redirect to the section's Build with a coding agent page. The fixed lines move out of view: the page shows only the text the reader edits. PLEX's fixed lines install the `composer-plugin-dev` skill into the folder, downloading `SKILL.md` and the files it links from the repository into the agent's own skills folder (`.claude/skills`, `.agents/skills` or `.cursor/skills`), then have the agent follow it; the copied prompt names all three folders. ECHO's fixed line has the agent read `/echo/llms-full.txt` first. The three open buttons are all primary, each in the palette color nearest its agent's brand: Claude Code in the property orange, Codex in the string blue, Cursor in the foreground neutral. The Notes example goes with the Open in Claude pages. Amends [D-116], [D-117] and [D-127].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.4, F-17.1, echo-build-with-agent, plex-build-with-agent]
  why: A reader should not need the `dxos` Claude Code plugin installed, or have to read a line they cannot change, and no one agent should look like the default.
  rejected:
    - Telling the agent to use the skill if installed and read it otherwise: it depends on the Claude Code plugin, and the other two agents have no way to install it.
```

```mdl
decision D-131: Each open button shows its agent's logo before its label, in the button's text color. The logos are Lobe Icons' monochrome SVGs (MIT), kept in `src/assets/agents/`. Amends [D-130].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-6.4]
  why: A reader finds their agent by its mark faster than by its name.
  rejected:
    - Simple Icons (CC0): it has the Claude and Cursor marks but dropped OpenAI's, and has no Codex mark.
```

```mdl
decision D-132: Build with a coding agent does not explain the buttons. Amends [D-130].
