  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [echo-build-with-agent, plex-build-with-agent]
  why: Pressing a button shows the whole prompt, fixed lines included, before anything is sent.
```

```mdl
decision D-133: Build with a coding agent targets Composer Preview (`https://preview.composer.space`), not composer.space, which loads only the plugins it ships with. The Composer address moves out of the editable prompt into PLEX's fixed lines, after the skill step, and the page says to sign in to Composer Preview first. Amends [D-127].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-build-with-agent]
  why: composer.space cannot load a plugin from a dev server, and a reader should not have to know which Composer to name.
```

```mdl
decision D-134: The PLEX page asks the reader to open an empty folder in their agent before pressing a button, and the prompt does not check the folder. Claude Code's link takes only an absolute `folder` path and Codex's an existing `path`; Cursor's takes none, and a web page cannot see the reader's files to fill one in. The skill sets the plugin up as its own repository with npm, so a folder inside a monorepo is not offered. Amends [D-130].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-build-with-agent]
  why: One sentence of setup works the same in all three agents.
  rejected:
    - A prompt step that stops when the folder is not empty: the reader is told what to do, and the step adds a line they did not ask for.
    - A folder field that fills `folder` and `path`: the folder must already exist, Cursor ignores it, and typing an absolute path is more work than opening the folder.
    - Having the agent make the folder: Codex's sandbox and Claude Code's permissions block or prompt on writes outside the open folder.
```

```mdl
decision D-135: The reader may open any folder, not only an empty one. When it is not empty, PLEX's fixed lines have the agent make a new folder for the plugin inside it: where the project keeps its packages, such as `packages/` in a monorepo, set up with the project's package manager, or else a folder named after the plugin. Amends [D-134].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-build-with-agent]
  why: A reader should be able to start from wherever their agent already is, and a new folder inside the open one stays within the agent's sandbox.
```

```mdl
decision D-136: The PLEX page assumes an empty folder again, and the fixed lines no longer have the agent make one. Placing a plugin inside an existing project, such as a monorepo, is follow-up work on the skill and this page. Reverts [D-135].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-build-with-agent]
  why: The skill sets a plugin up as its own repository with npm; a monorepo needs the skill changed first.
```

```mdl
decision D-137: The learning path does not embed StackBlitz in its pages. The ECHO object shows the finished app as the in-page embed, with Fork on StackBlitz; Installation, where the reader starts writing code, has Follow along in StackBlitz, which opens a starter with the learning path's code taken out. Both open in their own tab through the SDK's `openProject`, with files the docs build generates, so the docs need no isolation headers. To make the starter possible, each page's code moves from the standalone scripts in `src/tutorial/steps/` into the module of the app that runs it.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-15.6, F-15.7, F-15.8, F-15.9, the-echo-object, installation, defining-types, querying, mutating-objects, sharing]
  why: An inline StackBlitz embed needs `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` on the docs page, which restricts everything else the page loads, and in a 2026-11-11 test it ran only in WebKit; Chrome blocked its preview relay and Firefox's preview stayed blank.
  rejected:
    - A StackBlitz embed on every learning-path page that carries the reader's files from page to page: the isolation headers and browser support above.
    - A StackBlitz project from a GitHub folder: the starter would be a second committed copy of the app.
```

```mdl
decision D-138: The StackBlitz buttons post a form to `stackblitz.com/run`, the request the SDK's `openProject` sends, with the project's files in the page. The starter replaces each export in a quoted region with `todo('<page>, step <n>: <step>')`, and the app shows the stage the written pieces reach under a line naming the next step. `@dxos/*` pins pkg.pr.new commit `6bad7b6` of dxos#14487, its only published build, until that PR lands. Fills in [D-137].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-15.7, F-15.8, F-15.9]
  why: A click that first fetched the files or loaded the SDK would open the tab after an await, which browsers block as a popup; the files are about 60 KB and only two pages carry them.
  rejected:
    - Adding `@stackblitz/sdk` for one form post.
```

```mdl
decision D-139: Each StackBlitz button shows StackBlitz's bolt logo before its label, in the button's text color. The logo is Simple Icons' SVG (CC0), kept in `src/assets/brands/`. Amends [D-138].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-15.7, F-15.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-140: The tutorial app is one device: it opens its own space, and from Sharing a space on its toolbar has Invite, which copies a code, and Join, which takes one and switches the app to that space. The name and the online switch belong to a device frame the docs draw around each copy of the app, not to the app. Every embed shows one device except Sharing a space and The ECHO object, which show Alice's and Bob's side by side, each with a space of its own; only Alice's is seeded. The StackBlitz projects run the app as a real client, with no frame: `client.ts` configures EDGE and keeps the database in the browser's private file system, so a second browser can join, and the app reopens its space after a reload. The embeds keep their in-memory clients. Amends [D-137].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-15.3, F-15.7, F-15.8, installation, sharing, the-echo-object]
  why: The embeds mixed the demo's controls into the app, so the finished app lacked sharing and the second peer opened on a join screen no real app has; the StackBlitz project is where a reader builds a real app, which an in-memory network is not.
  rejected:
    - In-memory devices in StackBlitz too, which cannot share with anything outside the page.
```

```mdl
decision D-141: The PLEX learning path ends each page in a plugin inspector, not in Composer. The inspector is a PLEX app on an in-memory client that loads the reader's plugin at its stage, with one panel per kind of contribution; the docs embed it, StackBlitz runs it, and the plugin's dev server serves it.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-19, F-20, app-framework-create-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-surface, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph]
  why: Seeing a step land in Composer needs an account, Composer Preview and a dev server from the first page; the inspector shows each contribution on its own, in the page, and the reader keeps it after the docs.
  rejected:
    - A cut-down Composer in the embed, which hides most contributions behind navigation and needs the whole app to boot.
```

```mdl
decision D-142: The PLEX plugin is the path's first page: what a plugin is, the finished Bookmarks plugin in the inspector, and Fork on StackBlitz, as The ECHO object opens ECHO's path, so Create a plugin no longer shows it running. Follow along in StackBlitz is on Create a plugin.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-create-plugin, F-20.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-143: Composer comes in on Run it in Composer, the page before Publishing: Composer Preview, the dev server, the command palette and the assistant. Create a plugin no longer loads the plugin into a local Composer, and Publishing no longer covers developing against one.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-run-in-composer, app-framework-create-plugin, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-publishing]
```

```mdl
decision D-144: PLEX learning-path pages may use Effect where the PLEX API is Effect's, such as an operation handler written as `Effect.gen`. ECHO's pages stay with the promise APIs.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-add-operation, F-20]
```

```mdl
decision D-145: Installation documents every piece of `vite.config.ts` that ECHO needs in the browser: `vite-plugin-wasm` in the page and in `worker.plugins`, `build.target: 'esnext'`, `optimizeDeps.exclude` for `@dxos/wa-sqlite`, `@automerge/automerge` and `@automerge/automerge-subduction`, and `optimizeDeps.include` for the CommonJS modules only the database worker imports. The icon sprite's dist scan and the Tailwind source for `@dxos` stylesheets stay in the StackBlitz template without explanation, since they serve react-ui, which the docs use only for demonstration.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [installation]
```

```mdl
decision D-146: The PLEX learning path has no StackBlitz projects: The PLEX plugin has no Fork on StackBlitz and Create a plugin has no Follow along in StackBlitz. The reader builds the plugin in a local package, and the inspector drops the starter placeholder. Amends [D-141] and [D-142].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-19, F-20, plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-create-plugin]
  why: A plugin running in StackBlitz is served from StackBlitz's machine, where neither the docs inspector nor Composer can load it, so the reader would end up with a plugin they cannot carry into Run it in Composer.
```

```mdl
decision D-147: The inspector is a module workbench: a header with the plugin, its source and the sample object; a sidebar of modules with their status; and a main area showing the selected module working. Learning-path pages load the reader's own plugin from its dev server with Load dev plugin, and check it against what the page adds; only The PLEX plugin loads the finished plugin by itself. The dev server no longer serves the inspector. Amends [D-141].
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-19, F-20, plex-the-plex-plugin, app-framework-create-plugin, app-framework-define-type, app-framework-add-surface, app-framework-add-operation, app-framework-extend-app-graph, plex-run-in-composer]
  why: Tabs per kind of contribution, filled from the docs' own copy of the plugin, did not show the reader what their own code did; the path adds one module per page, so the modules are the natural index.
  rejected:
    - A mini Composer, with a nav tree, an article and a command palette: it hides translations, schema and skills, and shows nothing until the app graph page.
    - Serving the inspector from the plugin's dev server: the docs inspector reaches the dev server already.
```

```mdl
decision D-148: PLEX's Core concepts are Plugins and modules, Capabilities, Activation, Operations, Surfaces and App Graph, in that order. Anatomy of a plugin becomes Plugins and modules at `/docs/plex/concepts/plugins/`, and `/docs/plex/introduction/` redirects to it.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-anatomy, plex-capabilities, plex-activation, app-framework-operations, app-framework-surfaces, app-framework-app-graph]
  why: Anatomy of a plugin packed capabilities and activation into one page and still described the removed plugin context; a reader meets operations before surfaces on the learning path, so the concepts follow that order.
```

```mdl
decision D-149: "App Graph" is a proper name in PLEX prose: two words, capitalized, without "the". The namespace stays `AppGraph`, and the learning-path page is Extend the App Graph at the same route.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-app-graph, app-framework-guide-app-graph, app-framework-extend-app-graph, app-framework-glossary]
  why: It names one structure in the app, like ECHO or HALO, not a kind of graph.
```

```mdl
decision D-150: PLEX's API group adds PluginManager and Translations. AppGraph covers `AppNode` and `GraphPath`, and AppCapabilities is a tour in groups with one table, not a section per capability.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-guide-plugin-manager, plex-guide-translations, app-framework-guide-app-graph, app-framework-guide-app-capabilities]
  why: A reader loading plugins at runtime or writing strings had no page; AppCapabilities has too many members for one heading each.
```

```mdl
decision D-151: PLEX's Guides are Using ECHO in a plugin, Testing a plugin, Settings and state, Effect in plugins, Debugging a plugin and React. Using ECHO in a plugin is a guide, not a concept, because it joins ECHO and PLEX. The dx CLI stays later.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-guide-using-echo, plex-guide-testing, plex-guide-settings-and-state, plex-guide-effect, plex-guide-debugging, app-framework-guide-react, app-framework-cli]
  why: Each answers a task a plugin author hits after the learning path; registering ECHO types is integration work, not an idea of PLEX's own.
  rejected:
    - Objects in the app as a core concept: it is not a PLEX concept.
```

```mdl
decision D-152: The PLEX API reference covers `@dxos/app-framework`, `@dxos/app-toolkit`, `@dxos/app-graph` and `@dxos/compute`. Operation is documented from `@dxos/compute/Operation`, since `@dxos/operation` exports only the invoker.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-api-reference, app-framework-guide-operation]
  why: Those are the packages a plugin imports from.
```

```mdl
decision D-153: The plugin manifest is written, in Resources, at `/docs/plex/resources/manifest/`. Concept and API snippets come from the Bookmarks modules, except Plugin's, which keep World Clock [D-129], and concept pages may embed the inspector with the finished plugin.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-manifest, app-framework-operations, app-framework-surfaces, app-framework-app-graph]
  why: One plugin carried from the learning path into the reference lets a reader recognize each snippet.

decision D-200: PLEX's guides run in this order: Effect in plugins, Testing, Debugging, App capabilities, Settings and state, App Graph, React, Using ECHO in a plugin. Effect comes first because every module body and handler is an Effect.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [plex-guide-testing, plex-guide-debugging, plex-guide-settings-and-state, app-framework-guide-react, plex-guide-effect, plex-guide-using-echo]
  why: A reader works through the guides in order, so each should build on the last; ECHO is the most involved and goes last.

decision D-201: App Graph, AppCapabilities and Translations are app-level, not core PLEX. App Graph becomes one guide that explains the idea and the API, Translations folds into an App capabilities guide, and both sit in Guides; Core concepts and API keep only what `@dxos/app-framework` defines.
  date: 2026-11-11
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [app-framework-guide-app-graph, app-framework-guide-app-capabilities, app-framework-app-graph, plex-guide-translations]
  why: A PLEX app without App Graph is still a PLEX app; App Graph matters most of the app-level pieces, so it gets its own guide.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext template
  uri: org.dxos.docs.template@1.0
  desc: A page format, as the ordered parts every page of that template has.
  fields:
    purpose: Prose
    parts: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext page
  uri: org.dxos.docs.page@1.0
  desc: One page of the docs. The inline prose is its summary; the block's position sets its sidebar order.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    section: Prose
    route: URI
    group: Prose
    template: ExtRef
    status: planned | spike | done | later
    covers?: ProseList
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
